  "adaptations": [
    "This native workspace matches the supplied Bauhaus panel grid and primary-color hierarchy. Controls, values, curves, preset data and routes remain connected to the actual processor; the reference PNG is not used as a working interface.",
    "The main waveform tabs select the actual OSC 1, OSC 2 or OSC 3 preview without changing sound. A fictitious MIX preview is not shown. The separately labelled OSC 1 wavetable inset displays real copied source frames in perspective, while the large view uses ribbons.",
    "Each oscillator has a native algorithm menu, power/mute control and real previous/catalog/next wavetable selector. Non-wavetable algorithms disable table navigation. Four dynamic parameter labels follow the current oscillator algorithm.",
    "The envelope tabs select the two native scene envelopes or the real LFO 1/LFO 2 envelope stages; the same ADSR controls rebind safely. The last two choices are labelled LFO envelopes rather than fictional independent ENV 3/4 processors.",
    "Eight native FX cards select the detail editor. All five detail controls and the algorithm menu rebind to the selected slot. The initial Distortion view exposes real drive, pre-EQ frequency, output gain and high-cut parameters; current labels remain authoritative when algorithms change.",
    "Supported Distortion models display a cached native waveshaper transfer at the current drive. The preview is shaper-only, excluding EQ, feedback and output gain; other algorithms retain an honestly labelled category glyph. The full native editor retains all sixteen FX slots and specialized editors.",
    "The filter cards use real frequency-response previews, cutoff, resonance, envelope amount and key tracking. Envelope amount is not renamed Drive because the native shared waveshaper is a different control.",
    "Filter routing and mix use native parameters. The performance scene menu exposes native scene modes; the output slider adjusts selected scene level rather than inventing an A/B parameter morph.",
    "The browser uses the installed catalog. Reference-only category counts, preset descriptions and tags are not baked into the UI.",
    "The output plot and meters consume the real main-output tap. An inactive stream produces silence rather than invented spectrum activity.",
    "Measured rotary faces and centres, scene-row baselines and the compact voice-mode selector refine the native proportions against the supplied reference. Oscillator and effect labels remain dynamically derived from the current engine algorithm. Current-source native capture is required to assess remaining rendering differences."
  ]
}
